 "notes": "Blender: Z up, faces -Y, metres; GLB export +Y up (faces +Z in Godot). socket_offsets.loc are in the bone's own rest frame (Y = along the bone head->tail, Blender/Godot convention); socket_rest_world_* give the same points in model space. Necks are numbered left to right in the front view: 1-4 on the character's right (-X), 5-8 on its left (+X); on each side the outermost/lowest head is 1 (right) / 8 (left) and the inner top heads are 4 and 5, so mirror pairs are 1-8, 2-7, 3-6, 4-5. Leg bones: leg_<fl|fr|bl|br>_01 = shoulder/hip -> elbow/knee, _02 -> wrist/hock, _03 -> ankle, foot_* -> toe tip. Rest pose = the generated neutral pose. Bone rolls are 0: animate in armature-space angles. The jaw is fused in the mesh (no mouth interior): jaw_c opens the lower face by stretching, keep it within ~20 deg. The touching necks were ripped apart along their fused seams (vertices duplicated, no faces added), so a neck that leaves its neighbour shows a narrow open seam instead of a membrane: keep hydra_mat double-sided (glTF doubleSided = true -> Godot cull_mode disabled). Fix round 1: the headless 10th tube that stood behind the centre neck was deleted from the mesh (1,775 verts) and its opening capped; neck_c can now bend forward freely (each joint up to ~25 deg). The outer (back) side of the thick centre-neck base still stretches smoothly in a deep bow (no tear). head_down (jaw weak point, SPEC 3.3): neck bends alone cannot bring the head down (neck base 6.8 m, chain 5.6 m). Use the BOW in clip_recipes.head_down_bow: spine_01 +10, spine_02 +12, spine_03 +25, neck_c 25/25/20/15/10, head_c -30, front legs folded by IK so the front feet stay planted (leg_f*_01 -28, _02 -94, _03 +75; elbows stay behind), hind legs untouched. Result: jaw_c socket at z ~1.2 m, snout ~0.2 m above the ground, shoulders down ~1.45 m. Optionally let neck_4_01/neck_5_01 follow +10..15 deg. Target for the clip: jaw_c socket z <= 1.5 m. Scale (fix round 1, lead to confirm): kept at the brief's 6.5 m shoulder, so heads reach 12.2-13.5 m (centre horns 14.4 m) and nose-to-tail is 16.0 m, not SPEC 3.3's ~11 m heads / ~18 m; a x0.80 scale would give 11 m heads but a 5.2 m shoulder.",
